{title: 105 - Sing to the Great Jehovah's Praise}
{subtitle: SDA Hymnal #105 • LOBT GOTT IHR CHRISTEN • 8.6.8.7.7}
{lyricist: Charles Wesley}
{composer: Nikolaus Herman}
{key: Eb}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{meta: hymn_number 105}
{meta: tune LOBT GOTT IHR CHRISTEN}
{meta: meter 8.6.8.7.7}
{meta: category God the Father - }

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[Eb]Sing [Bb/D]to the [Eb]great Jehovah's [Bb7]praise!
[Bb/D]All [Cm]praise to [Bb]Him [Cm/Eb]belongs;
[Bb/D]Who [Eb]kindly [Gm]lengthens out [Ab]our days,
[Gm]In [Fm/C]spires [Bb]our [Cm]choicest songs,
[Eb]Inspires [Ab]our [Eb/Bb]choicest songs.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[Eb]His [Bb/D]providence [Eb/G]hath [Ab]brought [Bb7]us through
[Bb/D]Another various [Fm]year;
[Bb/D]We [Eb]all, [Bb7/F]with [Gm]vows [Cm]and [Gm]anthems [Ab]new,
[Gm]Before [Bb]our [Cm]God appear,
[Eb]Before [Ab]our God [Eb/Bb]appear.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[Eb]O [Bb/D]God, Thy [Eb]mercies [Ab]past [Bb7]we own,
[Bb/D]And [Cm]Thy continued [Fm]care;
[Bb/D]To [Eb]Thee [Bb7/F]presenting [Gm]through [Ab]Thy Son
[Gm]What [Fm/C]e'er [Bb]we [Cm]have and are,
[Eb]What [Ab/C]e'er we have [Eb/Bb]and [Bb7]are.
{end_of_verse}
